  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY THROUGH SUNDAY/...\nIssued at 116 AM CDT Mon Oct 12 2026\n\nWednesday through Sunday\nAssessment...a certainty (>97%) of a significant cool down\n\nThe first of two cold fronts will bring temperatures closer to \nnormal for Wednesday. Another storm system will bring likely\nchances (70-90 percent) of rain Wednesday night into Thursday.\n\nA much stronger cold front will sweep through the area Thursday \nnight and usher in below-normal temperatures to the area for \nFriday and the weekend.\n\nFriday will be windy and quite chilly. In spite of the much cooler \ntemperatures, the strong winds are expected to result in an elevated \nrisk of agricultural field fires.\n\nThe potential for frost continues to increase for the first half of \nthe weekend, especially Friday night.",
